/* A REAL RSA-2048 KEY, from `openssl genrsa`. Not three primes
   this script multiplied together: the point is that the
   kernel's arithmetic agrees with the library everybody else
   uses, on a key that library produced.

   BN_RSA_lam IS THE ONE TO CHECK bn_modinv AGAINST. openssl
   follows RFC 8017 and computes d = e^-1 mod lcm(p-1,q-1), not
   mod (p-1)(q-1). Both are working private exponents and both
